CDialogTree
{
Name=Broadcast Probe
Portrait=!None
Should Have Voiceovers=0
Default Canceled Node Action=
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=1 Conversation Start
Text=<PLAYTEST PROBE -- shared-name broadcast>  Option 1 is the control: it pacifies the warning troll, and exactly one entity carries that name. Option 2 is the test: it pacifies by the name fifteen generators share.  NOTE: thirteen more troll generators spawn with no name at all, so if the broadcast works you should see roughly HALF the pit ignore you, not all of it.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=1. CONTROL - pacify 'warning troll' (one entity has this name).
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CMultipleActionsAction
{
Action=Array
{
Item Count=2
Action=CSetTargetTypeAction
{
Entity Name=warning troll
Name To Target=
Valid Targets=
}
Action=CPrintCombatTextAction
{
Text to print=CONTROL fired. Now walk into his trigger. If he does NOT attack, single-name targeting works.
Character to show text to=$Instigator
Emphasize=1
Suppress Duplicates=0
}
}
}
Icon=Quest Icon

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=2. TEST - pacify 'Lava Troll' (fifteen entities share this name).
Go to node ID=
Custom Action=CMultipleActionsAction
{
Action=Array
{
Item Count=2
Action=CSetTargetTypeAction
{
Entity Name=Lava Troll
Name To Target=
Valid Targets=
}
Action=CPrintCombatTextAction
{
Text to print=BROADCAST fired. Walk the pit and count. Roughly half ignoring you = it broadcasts. None = it does not.
Character to show text to=$Instigator
Emphasize=1
Suppress Duplicates=0
}
}
}
Icon=Quest Icon

